====================================================================
FINDING 0 — FREEZE_WHILE_SMM IS ALREADY A ONE-LINE SYSFS TOGGLE ON THIS MACHINE
  $ ls /sys/devices/cpu/
    caps  events  format  freeze_on_smi  perf_event_mux_interval_ms  power
    rdpmc  subsystem  type  uevent
  $ cat /sys/devices/cpu/freeze_on_smi
    1
  MEASURED. The knob exists and is ALREADY ENABLED by default on Comet Lake.
  It writes IA32_DEBUGCTL[14]. Mainline since Kan Liang's 2017 series
  ("perf/x86: add sysfs entry to freeze counter on SMI"), whose stated rationale is
  verbatim: "in some cases, SMI cycles should not be counted -- for example, to
  calculate the cost of SMI itself."
  `perf stat --smi-cost` (man perf-stat) already implements the candidate's
  "corollary claim": it sets freeze_on_smi, then reports SMI cost as
  (aperf - unhalted_core_cycles)/aperf using msr/aperf/ and msr/smi/.
  -> The "strictly better instrument than MSR_SMI_COUNT, which counts events but
     not cost" is a flag that shipped nine years ago and is on by default here.

