    2000012 2000015 2000012 2000012
  DERIVED: (instructions - branches) = 16,000,030 in ALL 20 reps, exactly.
    Both counters are inflated by the SAME per-rep integer. That integer is 0 for
    the 11 reps that report the floor value. The floor IS the exact architectural
    count; the excess is the documented iret/interrupt overcount
    (Weaver/Terpstra/Moore, ISPASS 2013; Weaver's per-uarch table lists Core2,
    Atom, Nehalem, SandyBridge, AMD as "count is high by number of hardware
    interrupts").
  => min-of-N recovers the BIT-EXACT integer under a hosted OS, for free.

