====================================================================
ARCHITECTURAL OBJECTION — BARE METAL IS STRICTLY WORSE AT THIS
  IA32_FIXED_CTR_CTRL (0x38D) gates each fixed counter with EN_OS (CPL 0) and
  EN_USR (CPL > 0). The UEFI application runs entirely at CPL 0. Therefore:
    - EN_USR counts nothing.
    - EN_OS counts the workload AND the firmware's timer ISR body, with no way to
      separate them.
  And the firmware timer interrupt IS live: aegis-uefi never calls
  ExitBootServices and never raises TPL (grep-verified, zero matches; confirmed
  independently in skeptic_variance_budget_kill_2026-07-29.log), and it calls
  uefi::boot::stall at main.rs:79,158,245,398,406,414,675,766,824,881.
  A ~91.0 Mtick prefill at ratio 25 is ~41 ms of wall time. A UEFI firmware timer
  at the usual 100 Hz fires 4 or 5 times in that window depending on PHASE, not on
  the workload. Per Weaver's table the count is high by the number of hardware
  interrupts — and on bare metal it is additionally high by the whole ISR body.
  PREDICTION, PRE-REGISTERED: the candidate's own Stage-1 kill criterion
  ("if the five counts are not identical, the claim is DEAD") FAILS on the Dell,
  for a reason that has nothing to do with the workload's determinism.

====================================================================
CHEAPER KILL THAN THE SCOUT'S STAGE 0 — PURE CPUID, NO MSR, NO IDT
  FREEZE_WHILE_SMM may be set ONLY if IA32_PERF_CAPABILITIES(0x345).bit12 == 1,
  and 0x345 exists only if CPUID.01H:ECX[15] (PDCM) == 1. Setting the bit on a
  PerfMon V1 part can #GP — mainline carries a patch titled exactly
  "perf/x86/intel: Don't enable freeze-on-smi for PerfMon V1".
  The scout's Stage 0 reads CPUID.0AH but NOT PDCM and NOT 0x345[12]. Adding
  CPUID.01H:ECX[15] to the same banner is ~1 line and kills the entire SMM-tax arm
  on any machine that lacks PDCM — before the 150-line IDT is written.
  (Recorded for completeness: this box HAS pdcm. The Dell 06_3D and the HP Stream
  06_7A are unverified.)

